-- title:
--   Remark 3.21: Projection and translated central cone criteria
-- statement:
--   All vector spaces and Lie algebras are finite dimensional and real, with their usual Hausdorff topology. An invariant set is invariant under the group generated by $e^{\operatorname{ad}y}$. A closed convex set is pointed when its recession edge is zero. Write $\mathcal O_x=\operatorname{Inn}(\mathfrak g)x$, $\operatorname{co}(x)=\overline{\operatorname{conv}}\mathcal O_x$, and $C_x=\operatorname{cone}(\mathcal O_x)$. Admissibility means existence of a pointed generating invariant closed convex subset.
--
--   In the faithful admissible structural setting, pointedness of $\operatorname{co}(x)$ implies pointedness of the orbit hull of $x_l$ computed inside $\mathfrak l$. For $x_V=0$,
--
--   $$\operatorname{co}_z(x)=x_z+C_{x,z},\qquad\operatorname{co}_z(x)\text{ pointed}\iff C_{x,z}\text{ pointed}.$$
--
--   If these sets are pointed, containment of $\operatorname{co}_z(x)$ in a pointed cone is equivalent both to $(x_z+C_{x,z})\cap(-C_{x,z})\subseteq\{0\}$ and to that intersection being empty or $x_z=0$. These are conditional translated-cone criteria.
-- source:
--   Elements in pointed invariant cones in Lie algebras and corresponding affine pairs, arXiv:2110.07297v1, PDF p. 16, Remark 3.21: Projection and translated central cone criteria

import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Frontier30_P26

namespace QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Frontier30.P26

